ef 17592186045493 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420687 1077 "selection" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420687 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420633 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420687 1079 #uuid "dae23ffb-af9a-509a-99d1-3643141889bf" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420688 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420635 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420688 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420636 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420688 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420647 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420688 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420657 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420688 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420670 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420688 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420688 1077 "selection" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420688 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420635 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420688 1079 #uuid "ecfcee5e-24eb-56dc-ac84-c2b7a4109c97" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420689 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420680 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420689 1069 "q-216443" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420689 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420689 1071 "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}+7n+12=0$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n\n- $n\\ge -4$\n- $n=-4$\n- $|n|\\le 4$" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420689 1072 #uuid "00b6d002-6ca8-5b5f-a710-55bc4f02fb94" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420689 1074 "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\n$$\n\nNote that the solutions to the given equation are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}+7n+12 & =0 \\\\ (n+4)(n+3) & =0 \\\\ n & =-4,-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n\\ge -4)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=0,$ then $n\\ge -4,$ but ${n}^{2}+7n+12\\ne 0.$\n\n- Condition II is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n=-4)\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $n=-4,$ then ${n}^{2}+7n+12=0.$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(|n|\\le 4)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}+7n+12=0)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=0,$ then $|n|\\le 4,$ but ${n}^{2}+7n+12\\ne 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420690 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420681 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420690 1069 "q-172300" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420690 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420690 1071 "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}$ is an even number\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n\n- $n$ is an odd number\n- $n$ is a positive number\n- $n$ is a multiple of $2$" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420690 1072 #uuid "04618c03-3ca0-590d-b082-33d1176f03c4" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420690 1074 "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary* from the given one:\n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number})\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions. \n\n- Condition I is *not* a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number })\\,⇏\\,(n\\text{ is an odd number})\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $n=2$ is not an odd number but ${2}^{2}$ is an even number.\n\n- Condition II is *not* a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number})\\,⇏\\,(\\text{ is a positive number})\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the number $n=-2$ is not a positive number, but $(-2)^{2}$ is an even number.\n\n- Condition III is a necessary condition: \n\n$$\n({n}^{2}\\text{ is an even number})\\,⇒\\,(n\\text{ is a multiple of }2)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSince ${n}^{2}$ is even, it must also be true that $n$ is even. Therefore, $n$ is a multiple of $2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420691 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420682 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420691 1069 "q-172315" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420691 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420691 1071 "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}=16$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n\n- $n=4$\n- $-4<n<4$\n- $|n|<16$" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420691 1072 #uuid "10fd92b2-5e05-5850-b7d2-d8140b9fd04f" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420691 1074 "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}=16)\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {n}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ (n+4)(n-4) & =0 \\\\ n & =-4,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(n=4)\\,⇒\\,({n}^{2}=16)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $n=4,$ then ${n}^{2}=16.$\n\n- Condition II is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(-4<n<4)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}=16)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=-1,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2} & =(-1)^{2} \\\\  & =1\\ne 16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition III is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(|n|<16)\\,⇏\\,({n}^{2}=16)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $n=-1,$ then $|n|<16,$ but ${n}^{2}=1\\ne 16.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420692 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420672 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420692 1069 "q-172325" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420692 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420692 1071 "$\\,$ $x+1>4$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are sufficient for the above to be true?\n\n- $|x|>3$\n- $x>3$\n- $x>4$" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420692 1072 #uuid "28567992-ba7f-5623-ad07-13abe4be416c" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420692 1074 "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *sufficient* for the given one:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,(x+1>4)\n$$\n\nNote that the solution to the given equation is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & >4 \\\\ x & >3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(|x|>3)\\,⇏\\,(x+1>4)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, if $x=-4,$ then we have $x+1=-3≯4.$\n\n- Condition II is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(x>3)\\,⇒\\,(x+1>4)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $x>3,$ then $x+1>4.$\n\n- Condition III is a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n(x>4)\\,⇒\\,(x+1>4)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nIf $x>4,$ then  $x+1>5>4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420693 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420678 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420693 1069 "q-216459" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420693 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420693 1071 "$\\,$ ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary and sufficient for the above statement to be true?\n\n- $f$ is a differentiable function\n- $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$\n- $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C,$ for any $C\\in R$" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420693 1072 #uuid "390cc44c-87e5-5905-81de-8b4495a342fd" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420693 1074 "Given that the equivalence $P⇔Q$ is true, we have that $P$ is a *necessary and sufficient condition* for $Q.$  \n\nIn our case, we need to find the conditions that are *necessary and sufficient* for the given one. In other words,\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇒\\,\\text{Condition}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇐\\,\\text{Condition}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C\\in R$ is the arbitrary constant.\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given conditions.\n\n- Condition I is *not* a sufficient condition:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇍\\,(f\\text{ is a differentiable function})\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, the function $f(x)={e}^{x}$ is a differentiable function but ${f}^{′}(x)\\ne {sec}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n- Condition II is *not* a necessary condition:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇏\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nFor example, for the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1,$ the statement ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ is true but $f(x)\\ne \\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1.$\n\n- Condition III is both necessary and sufficient: The statement ${f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x$ is true *if and only if* $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C,$ for any $C\\in R.$\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇒\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇐\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,⇔\\,(f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420694 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420673 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420694 1069 "q-172302" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420694 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420694 1071 "$\\,$ ${n}^{2}$ is an odd number\n\nWhich of the following conditions are necessary for the above to be true?\n\n- $n$ is odd\n- $n$ is a multiple of $3$\n- $n$ is a multiple of $5$" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420694 1072 #uuid "4b376045-26da-55cb-becc-db924f8d2dac" 13194139534415 17592186045417 true] [17592186420694 1074 "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the follo